          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-32952",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "go-ntlmssp: go-ntlmssp: Denial of Service via malicious NTLM challenge"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "go-ntlmssp is a Go package that provides NTLM/Negotiate authentication over HTTP. Prior to version 0.1.1, a malicious NTLM challenge message can causes an slice out of bounds panic, which can crash any Go process using `ntlmssp.Negotiator` as an HTTP transport. Version 0.1.1 patches the issue."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-32952",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-32952\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: github.com/Azure/go-ntlmssp\nFixed Version: 0.1.1\nLink: [CVE-2026-32952](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-32952)\ngo-ntlmssp is a Go package that provides NTLM/Negotiate authentication over HTTP. Prior to version 0.1.1, a malicious NTLM challenge message can causes an slice out of bounds panic, which can crash any Go process using `ntlmssp.Negotiator` as an HTTP transport. Version 0.1.1 patches the issue.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-32952**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|github.com/Azure/go-ntlmssp|0.1.1|[CVE-2026-32952](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-32952)|\n\ngo-ntlmssp is a Go package that provides NTLM/Negotiate authentication over HTTP. Prior to version 0.1.1, a malicious NTLM challenge message can causes an slice out of bounds panic, which can crash any Go process using `ntlmssp.Negotiator` as an HTTP transport. Version 0.1.1 patches the issue."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 5.3,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:L",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.3",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-36308",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "disintegration Imaging 1.6.2 allows attackers to cause a panic (becaus ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "disintegration Imaging 1.6.2 allows attackers to cause a panic (because of an integer index out of range during a Grayscale call) via a crafted TIFF file to the scan function of scanner.go. NOTE: it is unclear whether there are common use cases in which this panic could have any security consequence"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2023-36308",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-36308\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: github.com/disintegration/imaging\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2023-36308](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2023-36308)\ndisintegration Imaging 1.6.2 allows attackers to cause a panic (because of an integer index out of range during a Grayscale call) via a crafted TIFF file to the scan function of scanner.go. NOTE: it is unclear whether there are common use cases in which this panic could have any security consequence",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-36308**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|github.com/disintegration/imaging||[CVE-2023-36308](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2023-36308)|\n\ndisintegration Imaging 1.6.2 allows attackers to cause a panic (because of an integer index out of range during a Grayscale call) via a crafted TIFF file to the scan function of scanner.go. NOTE: it is unclear whether there are common use cases in which this panic could have any security consequence"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
